(version 1)

# Custom design rules for hat-01. KiCad reads `<board>.kicad_dru` from the board's own directory;
# Board Setup → Design Rules → Custom Rules is an editor for this file, so opening that dialog and
# pressing OK will write back whatever it has buffered.
#
# A custom rule beats the netclass for the constraint it names. Where two rules match the same pair
# of objects, the *last* one in the file wins — so a rule added below this one and matching the
# same objects takes it over, not the other way round.
#
# This board carries no custom rules. The mounting hardware's copper keep-outs are rule areas on
# the board itself (`hat_hole_*`, Ø6.5 mm on F.Cu and B.Cu at each of the HAT's four holes),
# because the HAT land draws its holes on Edge.Cuts and nothing else keeps a screw head off a pour.
